# Citroen DS, 1962-1975.
#
# The second DS object, covering the Series 2 restyle of September 1962 and the
# Series 3 of late 1967 to the end of production in 1975. It is the same shell
# as the 1955-62 Series 1 car with a revised nose and rear, and was built as a
# variant of that master.
#
# Dimensions 4.826 x 1.791 x 1.464 m, wheelbase 3.124 m, as the Series 1 car.
# Source: the reference pack's notes (Wikipedia infobox). The modelled hull is
# 4.826 m long on the 3.124 m wheelbase and 1.788 m wide, about 3 mm narrower
# than the published figure after the variant's trim changes.
#
# **Which nose is modelled.** The Series 2 of 1962-67 kept the exposed round
# headlamps of the Series 1 car. The faired-in four-lamp glass canopy came with
# the Series 3 restyle of late 1967 for the 1968 model year, and that is the
# nose modelled here, because the reference pack's car is a 1973 DS 20. The
# Series 2's 1962-67 nose is therefore **not separately represented**; the
# object carries the 1962 intro date and the 1968 nose, the same convention used
# for the Corolla E120 and the Megane I.
#
# Shape reference: a true square-on side elevation, a front three-quarter and a
# rear three-quarter, all of the same UK 1973 DS 20. The teardrop body, roof,
# covered rear wheels and glazing are the Series 1 master's; the nose, bumper,
# lamps and rear details are changed to the photographs.
#
# Colours: no British-market colour list was found, so the objects carry plain
# names: black, white, red and blue. Weights black 3, white 3, red 2, blue 2,
# total 10, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 165 km/h, the DS 21's quoted maximum. Comfort 85/458, on the line
# 330 + 1.5 x 85: the hydropneumatic suspension and the later seats made it one
# of the most comfortable cars of its generation. Classes 2,3,4.
#
# Dates are road presence: September 1962 intro, retires staggered 1980-1983 on
# an eighteen- to twenty-one-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/citroen-ds-1962.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/citroen-ds-1962.dae (61 objects). References:
# citycars/references/citroen-ds-1962/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the inherited rear roof and glazing profile is more
# angular than the photograph, and the front canopy reads as separate lenses on
# a dark panel rather than a continuous glass cover. At 128 px the teardrop
# body, the covered rear wheels and the wide faired nose read as a later DS.

